From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 02:57:05 -0500
Subject: test: the tests of the 2026-11-22 code review's fixes

A review of every Stedding patch found 186 faults. Each fix went into the
patch that owns its code; their tests are here, one file per batch of
related fixes (audit_bNN_* for the first round, audit_w2_bNN_* for the
second), registered in the BUILD.gn files beside them with the deps they
need. Each test failed on the code before its fix and passed with it on
Windows; the Mac-only ones were proven on the Mac. The spec rows in
docs/features/ cite them.

Why: every fix of the review keeps a test that fails without it
(docs/AGENT-LOOP.md).
Removable when: never as a whole; a test goes with the behaviour it
checks, or moves into its feature's test file.
