+// P18-1c, routing D5, folders F37: "Always Open <site> in" on a tab inside a
+// folder files the tab in the other Space and takes it out of the folder
+// first, as Move to Space does, so the folder never spans two Spaces. It was
+// filed there and left in the folder, whose header then showed in both.
+TEST_F(RoutingB16Test, AlwaysOpenInTakesAFoldersTabOutOfTheFolder) {
