+// The Space switcher's chips under the pointer. A chip dragged to another
+// place moves its Space there and leaves the Space on screen as it was: the
+// drop is not a click on the chip (spaces B27). At overflow the chips stay
+// full size while the pointer is anywhere on the row, between two chips or
+// above or below one, not only while it is on a chip (spaces B25).
